%% Blindspot — BUILD DECISIONS LOG (not a runtime flow)
%% Records WHAT was chosen at each phase and WHY. Phase 7C checkpoint: 356cef0.
%% files: Blindspot-PRD.md, Handoff.MD, packages/core/src/model-registry.ts, packages/core/src/eval/queue.ts
%% granularity: summary
flowchart TD
  P0["Phase 0 · Monorepo skeleton — DONE"]:::done
  P0c["pnpm + Turborepo · Hono gateway · tsx dev · internal packages export raw .ts<br/>WHY: one toolchain, no dev build step, instant HMR; Hono is tiny and edge-portable so the<br/>gateway can later run as N stateless instances (PRD §8)"]:::why
  P0d["Worker: BullMQ on Redis, runs in-process for local dev until Phase 8<br/>WHY: keep the queue interface from day one so nothing changes later, but no second process to run yet"]:::why

  P05["Phase 0.5 · Postgres schema — DONE"]:::done
  P05c["Drizzle pg-core · uuid PKs · jsonb for policy_json + evidence_json · pgEnum for statuses<br/>WHY: typed SQL where one schema file drives BOTH migrations and TS types; jsonb keeps<br/>policy/evidence flexible without a migration per tweak"]:::why
  P05d["Zod lives in packages/shared as the SINGLE source of truth; db imports the inferred types<br/>WHY: gateway validates requests + db shapes rows from the SAME definitions (no drift)"]:::why
  P05e["Added api_keys (hash + shown-once prefix) beyond §9<br/>WHY: the gateway must map an incoming bs_live_ key → project; never store raw keys"]:::why

  P1["Phase 1 · Gateway routing + adapters + trace — DONE"]:::done
  P1a["OpenAI-compatible POST /v1/chat/completions; model = route:name<br/>WHY: users just repoint base_url + swap the model string — zero SDK change to adopt (PRD §4)"]:::why
  P1b["Auth: bs_live_ key → sha256 hash lookup → project; raw key shown once at bootstrap<br/>WHY: a leaked DB never exposes usable keys; standard API-key hygiene"]:::why
  P1c["BYO provider keys AES-256-GCM at rest; decrypted in-memory per call only<br/>WHY: PRD §5 non-negotiable — user controls spend, zero markup, keys never logged"]:::why
  P1d["Adapters via Vercel AI SDK v4 — anthropic/openai/google/groq native, HF via OpenAI-compatible baseURL<br/>WHY: one interface for every provider (PRD stack); adding a provider = one switch case"]:::why
  P1e["Auto-create route from traffic, seed default model as first candidate; NEVER switch an existing<br/>route's live model here<br/>WHY: routes appear automatically (PRD §4 step 2); swaps are approval-gated only (§3)"]:::why
  P1f["Trace every call: cost (cents) · latency · output<br/>WHY: this is the Observe step; every later eval/drig decision reads these rows (PRD §6)"]:::why

  P2["Phase 2 · Golden sets (upload + agent) — DONE"]:::done
  P2a["New @blindspot/core package holds domain services (golden, later eval/policy)<br/>WHY: gateway + worker + dashboard all reuse ONE implementation, no logic in HTTP handlers"]:::why
  P2b["Seed two ways: upload CSV/JSONL (csv-parse + Zod) OR Golden Set Agent via generateObject<br/>WHY: PRD §7 upload-optional — schema-validated agent output means no brittle JSON parsing"]:::why
  P2c["Versioned sets (nextVersion), full CRUD, promote-a-trace; grow-from-production deferred<br/>WHY: score history stays comparable across versions; curate is the human-in-the-loop control"]:::why

  P3["Phase 3 · Eval engine (LLM-as-judge) — DONE"]:::done
  P3a["judgeOutput via generateObject (schema-validated verdict); runEval scores every active<br/>golden example then persists an eval_runs row<br/>WHY: reproducible, structured scores; the aggregate row is what policy + drift read"]:::why
  P3b["enqueueEval: BLINDSPOT_EVAL_MODE=inline explicitly bypasses Redis; otherwise BullMQ<br/>when REDIS_URL is set, inline when absent<br/>WHY: local work can pause Redis without changing production queue wiring"]:::why

  P4["Phase 4 · Recommendations + approvals — DONE"]:::done
  P4a["Policy = cheapest candidate with latest score >= bar AND cheaper than live; emits a<br/>Recommendation with evidence (scores + cost/latency deltas)<br/>WHY: PRD §3 — evidence-backed proposal, dedup pending recs per target"]:::why
  P4b["Approve → routes.live_model switches; Reject → status + reason stored; auto_approve (default OFF)<br/>applies within-band+cheaper swaps automatically, still logged<br/>WHY: §3 non-negotiable — no silent swap; reason tunes future recs"]:::why
  P4c["Phase 7C closed the evidence gap: every evaluated example stores candidate output,<br/>score, criteria, reasoning, issues, latency and candidate/judge cost<br/>WHY: Recommendations and route debugging must show the proof, not only an average"]:::done

  P3fix["🐞 FIX (found via live smoke test): eval scores were ~0.15 because the Golden Set Agent<br/>emitted BARE passages; runEval sent them with no instruction so candidates never did the task<br/>WHY the fix: golden inputs must be SELF-CONTAINED prompts (instruction embedded) — matches a<br/>real app call / promoted trace. After fix: 8B 0.16 → 0.89, and an approved swap flipped the live model"]:::why

  P5["Phase 5 · Drift + CI gate — DONE"]:::done
  P5a["checkDrift: re-eval (or simulated version-bump score) vs prior; if below margin or bar →<br/>drift_event + recovery recommendation (mode=drift picks best passing, cost secondary)<br/>WHY: PRD §5 — quality regressions surface as approval-gated recs, never silent reverts"]:::why
  P5b["Legacy paid drift + CI endpoints return 409 until Phase 8 can consume an approved queued plan<br/>WHY: a second endpoint must never bypass Phase 7C spend authorization"]:::why

  DONE["✅ Backend loop VERIFIED LIVE end-to-end (Groq + live Postgres):<br/>connect → route → trace → golden(agent) → eval(judge) → recommend → approve → live swap;<br/>drift detected; gate blocked a sub-bar model with 422"]:::done
  P7["Phase 7 · Dashboard (Next.js §10) — DONE"]:::done
  P7A["Phase 7A · Connect + Observe — DONE"]:::done
  P7Aa["Observe-only TypeScript SDK + authenticated batch ingestion; metadata-only default<br/>WHY: connect an existing agent without forcing it through Blindspot routing or retaining content"]:::why
  P7Ab["Workflow/node hierarchy links generation nodes to existing Routes; user selects workflows<br/>WHY: compatibility and optimization are node-specific, and discovery must not imply permission to change"]:::why
  P7Ac["Claude Sonnet 4.6 vs Haiku 4.5 first; HF + Fireworks adapters remain pluggable<br/>WHY: prove the end-to-end decision with gstpilot before widening the catalog"]:::why
  P7B["Phase 7B · Registry + Compatibility — DONE"]:::done
  P7Ba["Read-only provider catalog sync stores project-scoped account availability + normalized<br/>capabilities; listing consumes zero inference tokens<br/>WHY: expose only models the user's own account can actually access"]:::why
  P7Bb["Observed node requirements deterministically gate Sonnet/Haiku; excluded models carry reasons<br/>WHY: technical fit permits an experiment, while quality and spend remain separate later gates"]:::why
  P7Bc["Adding a compatible candidate does not run an eval or change live_model<br/>WHY: Phase 7C must estimate cost and obtain explicit spend approval before paid work"]:::why
  P7C["Phase 7C · Quality + Experiment — DONE LOCALLY"]:::done
  P7Ca["Immutable 30-minute eval plan: full estimate or disclosed SHA-seeded stratified sample;<br/>selected + omitted cases, calls, cost, safety and confidence shown before confirm<br/>WHY: the user owns eval spend and must know exactly what a smaller budget changes"]:::why
  P7Cb["Confirmation locks the plan once; every real eval requires its route/model/example authorization;<br/>per-example evidence is persisted immediately and incomplete runs cannot recommend<br/>WHY: budget, retry safety and evidence integrity are server-enforced, not UI conventions"]:::why
  P7Cc["Local mode runs inline with Redis bypassed; Phase 8 owns queued plan handoff, crash recovery,<br/>rate limits, observability and plan-aware CI/drift jobs<br/>WHY: preserve the approved scale architecture without depending on Redis for this prototype"]:::why

